{"event_type":"review","id":"9d89b18fa40ec32e17407b310f00b6ee2e759c6a39169fe9c02e65f8ba2d97c5","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T00:56:14Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b481c6ffe05dc022f0e1672dc434c3d5bb0d08739c16e45f2fb7e595359d23d6","sha256":"b481c6ffe05dc022f0e1672dc434c3d5bb0d08739c16e45f2fb7e595359d23d6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5ecdad98d07a0b641990a494292d8ae85b25ef7ced46773d8d392f156bf0acfb","sha256":"5ecdad98d07a0b641990a494292d8ae85b25ef7ced46773d8d392f156bf0acfb"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/fd09d7aefd5ca75994386dab944415a7b3efaeba40920bfe072397559799de94","sha256":"fd09d7aefd5ca75994386dab944415a7b3efaeba40920bfe072397559799de94"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/256fb58e097f13c8d795d80760c45a0250d79911226af24273edad458af30303","sha256":"256fb58e097f13c8d795d80760c45a0250d79911226af24273edad458af30303"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5b75956c754772a51d197fff7ab187d5ba7dac75ca0ea5bd7028281e38312dbb","sha256":"5b75956c754772a51d197fff7ab187d5ba7dac75ca0ea5bd7028281e38312dbb"}],"attempt_id":"8c85aacd9b3371c6f704537b3dc21b02e359b5541832557d85e336b954edf7a7:0:1","base":"296d5779a104ea7735e9c07e0edca8244e6fcb72","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"def167638a77d828b3d9d558115ee1a95f502fb1","body":"**Filter address-only checks from both input paths.**\n\n`resolveChecks` skips `addressOnly` only when it reads the config file. If a caller passes the same configured `CqCheck[]` as `input.checks`, Line 126 returns the address-only checks for repository-wide execution. Apply the filter to explicit checks too, and reject an empty result in both paths.","id":"712049b6dbb89e3871062e79a380878a2cb83f1b104e89adc52cd6eba174caec","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/analyze/run.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Filter address-only checks from both input paths."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"2ef144374426e7ffb237fa6479c1fc75dae85c3d","body":"**Normalize paths before selecting tests.**\n\nOn Windows, `relative()` returns backslash-separated changed paths. Recursive test discovery can also return backslash-separated paths. The selector and `isTest` match `/`, so a source change can produce an empty selection and a reported pass without running tests. Convert both paths to repository-relative POSIX paths, as `scripts/test-narrow.mjs` does for discovery. ([github.com](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/api/path.md?utm_source=openai))   \n\n\nAlso applies to: 22-23","id":"2d592c212c1f58a2c67b36739608e966ca80689bea174c62bb5d5e6d1ae6faf8","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/check-related-tests.mjs","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Normalize paths before selecting tests."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f6b0a4492cae99c26eba2024ac36acff5bff332b","body":"**Require a boundary after the source stem.**\n\nIn `scripts/lib/related-tests.mjs:14`, a change to `src/ops/analyze/run.ts` can select an unrelated `test/ops/analyze/runtime.test.ts`. Allow both dot and hyphen suffixes so `check-affected.test.ts` remains selected. Update the twelve-file fixture to use dot-separated suffixes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n`scripts/lib/related-tests.mjs`:\n\n```diff\n-        if (test.startsWith(prefix) && !test.slice(prefix.length).includes('/')) selected.add(test);\n+        if (test.startsWith(prefix) && ['.', '-'].includes(test[prefix.length]) && !test.slice(prefix.length).includes('/')) selected.add(test);\n```\n\n`test/scripts/affected-tests.test.ts`:\n\n```diff\n     'test/ops/dev/check-affected.test.ts',\n     'test/ops/review/run.deadline.test.ts',\n+    'test/ops/dev/checker.test.ts',\n```\n\n```diff\n-    const files = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => `test/a${i}.test.ts`);\n+    const files = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => `test/a.${i}.test.ts`);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"c3238df733bb13b1352bd43d1865a681171182b5d38b85013250196143badf26","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/related-tests.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Require a boundary after the source stem."}],"head":"0420e90fbc77f8bdeb269122cd8e4b1c10e03f72","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"2ef144374426e7ffb237fa6479c1fc75dae85c3d","intervals":[[1,40]],"path":"scripts/check-related-tests.mjs"},{"blob":"f84c855dac2f628914d2a08f4aaf0621c8be7fa1","intervals":[[19,20]],"path":"scripts/lib/affected-tests.mjs"},{"blob":"09df78e3800d7af837d26143b22e0c3263e4131e","intervals":[[1,8]],"path":"scripts/lib/related-tests.d.mts"},{"blob":"f6b0a4492cae99c26eba2024ac36acff5bff332b","intervals":[[1,26]],"path":"scripts/lib/related-tests.mjs"},{"blob":"b269c54f0f50f17699c6498ea20039a24e4f5183","intervals":[[234,234],[239,239],[246,246],[562,568]],"path":"scripts/test-narrow.mjs"},{"blob":"cde303aa1901dbea6aa671309fdf4d6e49aa7c58","intervals":[[69,70],[161,161]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/cqConfig.ts"},{"blob":"c89577264898671634b9a39307ffa97a689e0581","intervals":[[28,31]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/cqConfigDefaults.ts"},{"blob":"def167638a77d828b3d9d558115ee1a95f502fb1","intervals":[[145,153],[156,156]],"path":"src/ops/analyze/run.ts"}],"job_id":"8c85aacd9b3371c6f704537b3dc21b02e359b5541832557d85e336b954edf7a7:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"e34586c0fc1d5467fe9e2cfa1d839a1197f775c9","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34864ea555846cd40945d9a27dd10f2241ecf2ba","source_path":"scripts/check-related-tests.mjs"},"blob":"2ef144374426e7ffb237fa6479c1fc75dae85c3d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"scripts/check-related-tests.mjs","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"ebda487ff0a1e84c9da